    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Brice Turang** standing out as the clear elite play (75.04). His matchup against Freeland provides the perfect storm: a significant park factor boost (+14%) and a high stolen base probability due to the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which maximizes his efficiency in our scarcity-driven roster strategy. Similarly, **Corbin Carroll** (71.43) remains a foundational start in the two-hole against Cavalli, benefiting from a favorable platoon advantage and high-leverage order placement. While **Jose Caballero** sits lower in the order, his 60.63 score is bolstered by a massive 13% platoon boost against the southpaw, making him a sneaky-high upside play for speed production despite the lower lineup protection.\n\nConversely, the lineup construction faced a tight squeeze at the margins, most notably with **Travis Bazzana**. He finished on the bench (42.86) as the odd man out, primarily because he is staring down a nightmare matchup against deGrom; even with his leadoff spot, the -19% SP skill penalty proved insurmountable. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Seiya Suzuki** (45.02) and **Dalton Rushing** (49.23), as both are facing tough opposing arms in McDonald and Soriano, respectively. **Vinnie Pasquantino** also carries risk (48.14) due to the -15% platoon penalty against the lefty Prielipp, but his base power profile keeps him marginally viable over available bench depth. We are monitoring the status of **Mickey Moniak**, who remains unavailable on the IL, while the rest of our depth like **Austin Riley** and **Alex Freeland** will remain in reserve, failing to crack the starting nine due to unfavorable matchups or inferior projected run-creation efficiency relative to the active starters.",
